## Result 3 isn't proof that the new bucket works

Your account couldn't read the new bucket's views earlier. So the entries in result 3 may come from `_Default`, written before you disabled it, and not from the new bucket at all. One hint: `careernavigator-frontend-staging-error.log` was written at 07:07, inside the 15-minute window, yet `frontend_apache_error` doesn't appear in the output. That fits "entries from before the disable".

I can't tell which it is. The disable time settles it:
```bash
P=pg-ae-n-app-125609
D=$(gcloud logging sinks describe _Default --project=$P --format="value(updateTime)")
echo "default disabled at: $D"; date -u
gcloud logging read 'logName:"logs/backend_" OR logName:"logs/frontend_"' --project=$P --limit=1 --format="value(timestamp,logName.basename())"
gcloud logging read "(logName:\"logs/backend_\" OR logName:\"logs/frontend_\") AND timestamp>=\"$D\"" --project=$P --limit=3 --format="value(timestamp,logName.basename())"
```
- **Entries after the disable time appear:** your account reads logs written after the disable, so they come from the new bucket, and routing works.
- **None appear while the servers are live:** either the new bucket isn't receiving, or your account can't read it. Open Logging → Logs Storage and look at the size of `cn-staging-logs-me2`. If it isn't growing, **re-enable `_Default` now** (Log Router → `_Default` → ⋮ → Enable sink), because logs are being lost.

The storage size in the Console is the one proof I can't get from a command, and I've asked for it before. Please look at it.

